<!--
    App.xaml — application-level resources only.

    StartupUri is deliberately absent. The window is created by the host in App.xaml.cs after the
    DI container is built, because MainWindow needs a ShellViewModel and ShellViewModel needs a
    pipe client that has to be disposed on exit. Letting XAML construct the window first would
    mean either a parameterless view model or a static service locator, and both put the
    dashboard's only route to the service outside the container.

    Dictionary order is load-bearing, and the palette must be FIRST: ThemeService replaces index 0 at
    runtime to switch light/dark, and it identifies the slot by looking for a palette key before
    touching it. Everything after it is ordered by what references what, because a StaticResource can
    only see keys declared before it:

      0  Palette.Dark   colour only, and the slot ThemeService swaps
      1  Metrics        spacing, radius and duration tokens; references nothing
      2  Icons          vector geometry; references nothing
      3  Animations     storyboards and easing; references nothing
      4  Theme          styles and control templates; references all four above
      5  PageTemplates  data templates; references Theme's styles

    Adding a dictionary above Palette.Dark would silently break the theme switch. ThemeService guards
    against it — it checks for the Surface.Page marker key and inserts rather than overwrites if the
    slot is wrong — but the guard logs a warning and leaves a duplicate palette merged, so the order
    here is still the thing to get right.

    Dark is the startup palette rather than the user's stored choice, because resources are merged
    before the container exists and ThemeService cannot read settings.json this early. It applies the
    real preference during startup, before the window is shown, so no flash is visible.
-->
<Application x:Class="AppGuardian.UI.App"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
  <Application.Resources>
    <ResourceDictionary>
      <ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
        <ResourceDictionary Source="Views/Palette.Dark.xaml" />
        <ResourceDictionary Source="Views/Metrics.xaml" />
        <ResourceDictionary Source="Views/Icons.xaml" />
        <ResourceDictionary Source="Views/Animations.xaml" />
        <ResourceDictionary Source="Views/Theme.xaml" />
        <ResourceDictionary Source="Views/PageTemplates.xaml" />
      </ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
    </ResourceDictionary>
  </Application.Resources>
</Application>
